  "qualification": "Incomplete experimental live-send mode; three uninstrumented startup failures remain unexplained. Existing accepted-queue gate passes on the same final source.",
  "candidate": {
    "head": "18f6e327addc63707736c91040524bdc734a323c",
    "sourceBefore": "8c709893142930ff518bf35ee73f983607bba9c914c881a7e94b4f6297d79ff4",
    "buildId": "v1THgZr1dvmIVuJQomLJ5",
    "sourceAfter": "8c709893142930ff518bf35ee73f983607bba9c914c881a7e94b4f6297d79ff4"
  },
  "implementation": [
    "Optional --live-ui-send runs the actual composer/send path from an empty isolated phone thread.",
    "Relaunch uses the normal ThreadSnapshotStore and AppModel hydration; no accepted delivery or response is reseeded.",
    "Controller verifies the real partial phone snapshot before termination, then saved server turn and exact run ID before restart.",
    "Recovered snapshot must retain user/assistant message IDs, clear the queue, restore summaries/tool/model and leave the durable counter at one provider request and one marker read.",
    "Production supervisor, authentication, recovery and notification code are unchanged. Temporary Swift diagnostics were removed."
  ],
  "observations": [
    "Initial, final and recheck runs fail opening the fixture chat, before any provider request or tool read. The first retained screenshot shows the connection screen. No auth-root-cause or product fix is established.",
    "A temporary Swift diagnostic run and a passive server request-observer run pass the complete live-send/termination/restart/hydration path. These passes do not supersede the failed uninstrumented attempts.",
    "The observer run sees authorized native requests succeed and the expired replay stream return 404 before authenticated history/output recovery.",
    "The observer running-state capture shows a native notification permission prompt. Accessibility presence is not unobscured visual acceptance."
  ],
